==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the injectivity constraint on forAttempt. The injected violation forces two distinct AuditEntries to share the same AccessAttempt, exactly the 'one entry was mutated/replaced by another' scenario the AppendOnly and FR_010 assertions are designed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_010_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_010_AuditImmutable: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompletenessForLookup  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompletenessForLookup.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the requirement that every LookupRecord AccessAttempt produces exactly one AuditEntry. The injection forces a LookupRecord attempt with Permitted outcome to have no corresponding AuditEntry — a record was observed without an audit trail, violating SC-001/SC-002.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_013_AuditSLAEnforced
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditSLAEnforced: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the biconditional that ties Permitted outcomes to active care-team memberships. The injection forces a Permitted AccessAttempt for which no active CareTeamMembership exists — a clinician outside the care team successfully reads a patient record, violating FR-006 and SC-010.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoInformationLeakageResponse  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_NoInformationLeakageResponse.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the constraint that Denied and NotFoundOrDenied must map to NotFoundShape. The injection forces a Denied outcome to carry SuccessShape, distinguishing 'patient exists but you cannot see it' from 'patient not found', leaking patient existence to an unauthorised caller.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_007_ByteEquivalentDenied
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ByteEquivalentDenied: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the requirement that an AuditEntry's recordedRole matches the caller's actual role. The injection forces an entry whose recorded role differs from the caller's role — a mis-attribution that would produce a misleading audit trail for IG investigators.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_009_AuditFields
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_AuditFields: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission matrix fact leaves Allowed unconstrained. The injection explicitly adds AuditOfficer -> LookupRecord to the matrix, which violates LeastPrivilege (IG officer gains patient-record access), PrivilegeMonotonicity (roles are no longer disjoint), FR_011 (SearchAudit exclusivity broken), and PermissionCompleteness (#Allowed > 5).
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PrivilegeMonotonicity, FR_011_IGRoleOnlyAuditSearch, PermissionCompleteness
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - PrivilegeMonotonicity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_IGRoleOnlyAuditSearch: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

